&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I recently stumbled upon a Twitter conversation that deeply resonated with some of my own &amp;ldquo;pains&amp;rdquo; as a developer. It was about the frustration of working in TypeScript and missing certain syntax features that make life so much sweeter in Dart.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&amp;rsquo;ve ever felt like you were &amp;ldquo;dying of thirst&amp;rdquo; looking for an elegant way to handle conditionals or build lists in TypeScript, you are not alone. Today, we&amp;rsquo;ll explore two of those features that make Dart feel so ergonomic: &lt;strong&gt;Switch Expressions&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Collection Control Flow&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Solving Artifacts with `ImageFilter.blur` in Flutter on Android, iOS and macOS</title><link>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/solving-artifacts-imagefilter-blur-flutter/</link><pubDate>Sun, 27 Oct 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/solving-artifacts-imagefilter-blur-flutter/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="solving-artifacts-with-imagefilterblur-in-flutter-on-android-ios-and-macos"&gt;
 Solving Artifacts with &lt;code&gt;ImageFilter.blur&lt;/code&gt; in Flutter on Android, iOS and macOS
